{
 "about": "10CL016 LAB control-line input mux, local LE sources (offline; xdev design ffc:KIND:S). Control signal from the LE at slot S of the same LAB drives one control of all 4 registers in LEs 0-3. Value: [frame offset, byte offset] relative to LE N0 (LUT frame 0, low byte, LUT plane), the bits in the control column (bytes -37..-27, frames -14..11) that depend on S, i.e. minus the bits common to all slots. Only slots where X10Y10 and X22Y8 agree are listed. sclr and ena share the mux code; aclr and clk codes barely depend on S (they arrive over another path). Not tested on silicon. ena and sclr codes differ in one bit: (-4,-31) for slots whose local line reaches LUT input 0 directly (li_direct.json), (-10,-31) for those reaching input 1 (9/9 slots), so the control mux has two entry points with the same reach as LUT inputs 0/1.",
